id:                     E350
trigger_tool:           runtime|bash|test
phase:                  runtime
error_signature:        Requirement plasma-activities-cli missing|xdpyinfo: not found|kdialog: not found

severity:               2
category:               portability, desktop-integration, provider-abstraction
match_keywords:         desktop wrapper, KDE Activities, plasma-activities-cli, xdpyinfo, kdialog, explicit context provider, OpenHarmony
title:                  Desktop wrapper hard-codes KDE/X11 services unavailable on OpenHarmony

root_cause:             Linux desktop wrapper hard-codes KDE Activities, X11 geometry and GUI dialog commands; OpenHarmony and other non-KDE desktops expose neither the same activity service nor the same display utilities.
affected_scope:         Shell and command-line wrappers that derive application state from KDE Activities, X11 geometry, desktop dialogs, notifications, portals, session managers, or similar desktop-specific commands.
verification_cmd:       bash test_activity_context.sh /path/to/packaged/activityfirefox

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           explicit-context-provider
rec_description:        Preserve native desktop auto-discovery when available, but move identity resolution behind a provider boundary and accept explicit ID/name inputs from OpenHarmony launchers or system-parameter bridges; restrict path-bearing IDs to a documented safe alphabet and length; make display/dialog helpers optional; test both resolution and the wrapped application flow.
rec_command:            patch -p1 < patches/0001-activityfirefox.patch && bash test_activity_context.sh /path/to/packaged/activityfirefox
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      single-default-context
fallback_description:   Use one documented stable default context only when the product explicitly does not need per-workspace separation.
fallback_command:       ACTIVITY_AWARE_ID=default ACTIVITY_AWARE_NAME=Default activityfirefox
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       fake plasma-activities-cli|hard-code random UUID|skip context resolution test|allow path separators in context ID
forbid_1_reason:        A command stub, unstable identifier, unsafe path component, or probe-only test does not implement a safe end-to-end platform contract.
forbid_1_consequence:   User data can be routed to the wrong Firefox profile, escape the profile directory, or produce a false-positive CI result.

principles:
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

